-- A DECLARED `of` enumeration that is over the materialization budget, so it
-- routes to the plan-guided lazy path instead of dense enumeration (task
-- of-annotation-forces-dense-enumeration). The domain this annotation names has
-- 21845 inhabitants (N_k = 1 + 4*N_{k-1}, N_0 = 1, at depth 7), over the 10000
-- of `defaultMaterializationCardinality`, so `enumerateAppliedLambda` declines
-- and dispatch falls through to `planWitnessApply`.
--
-- Before the budget gate the `of` annotation alone forced dense enumeration and
-- hid the plan path -- a pessimization switch, measured at 423x on this very
-- program at depth 8 (27,080,216 bytes emitted with the annotation against
-- 63,942 without it, the two being semantically identical).
--
-- ORACLE for the expected values below: the same program with the `of` line
-- deleted. That variant has no DiscreteValues tag, so it has always taken the
-- plan path and is untouched by the gate; at these logits it answers
-- p(1) = 0.03941878760821129 and p(0) = 0.9605812123917887, and the two
-- programs now emit byte-identical modules. Dense enumeration over the full
-- 21845-value domain agrees to within a few ulps (0.9605812123917892 /
-- 0.03941878760821113) -- the difference is summation order, 21845 accumulated
-- terms against the value-grouped DP, not a difference in meaning.
data Color = Red | Green | Blue
data Object = NoObj | Obj color::Color
data Scene = Empty | SCons obj::Object, rest::Scene depth 7

neural readScene :: (Symbol -> Scene) of 7x.{Empty | SCons {NoObj | Obj {Red|Green|Blue}} x}

numRed s = if isEmpty s then 0.0 else (if isObj (obj s) then (if isRed (color (obj s)) then 1.0 else 0.0) else 0.0) + numRed (rest s)

main sym = let scene = readScene sym in if numRed scene > 1.5 then 1 else 0
